From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 port
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Scheduler: EDEN_NX2_END_FAIL_SOFT=1 drops a command buffer the driver cannot end

Core patch on the T28 core (t27core, through 0413); applies with git apply on
src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp. Off unless asked for.

Run 102 (Mario Kart, T27, the run 101 env): at the course load, 195 s, vkEndCommandBuffer answered
VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY (report: vulkan_wrapper.h:1274 End x1). vk::Check threw, nothing on the
worker thread caught it, and the app stopped itself with the pool at 0 MiB largest. Run 101 crossed
the same shortage 30 s earlier in its menus and raced for 77 s more with images refused and unbacked.
The bad_alloc fallbacks (0181) cover pipelines and uploads, not this.

With the switch the two command buffers that failed are dropped, two empty ones carry the signal and
wait semaphores, and the tick is submitted as before, so every wait on it completes. The dropped
buffer's draws, uploads and downloads are lost: a wrong frame, and a download that leaves stale bytes
in the guest's memory, are possible. The pool is still empty afterwards; this only turns a sure end
into the state run 101 lived in. The log says "Command buffer could not be ended" with a count.

Syntax-checked with clang -fsyntax-only against the T28 core and the port's deps. Not built, not run.
---
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp
@@ -523,8 +523,41 @@
             .dstAccessMask = VK_ACCESS_MEMORY_READ_BIT | VK_ACCESS_MEMORY_WRITE_BIT,
         };
         upload_cmdbuf.PipelineBarrier(VK_PIPELINE_STAGE_TRANSFER_BIT, VK_PIPELINE_STAGE_ALL_COMMANDS_BIT, 0, WRITE_BARRIER);
-        upload_cmdbuf.End();
-        cmdbuf.End();
+        // EDEN_NX2_END_FAIL_SOFT=1: a command buffer the driver cannot end is dropped instead of
+        // ending the session. Run 102 (Mario Kart, T27): vkEndCommandBuffer answered
+        // VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY at the course load, the exception left the worker thread,
+        // and the app stopped itself; run 101 lived through the same shortage and raced. Two empty
+        // buffers carry the semaphores, so every wait on this tick still completes. The dropped
+        // buffer's draws, uploads and downloads are lost: a wrong frame, and a readback that
+        // brings stale bytes to the guest, are possible. Off unless asked for.
+        static const bool end_fail_soft = [] {
+            const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_END_FAIL_SOFT");
+            return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+        }();
+        try {
+            upload_cmdbuf.End();
+            cmdbuf.End();
+        } catch (const vk::Exception& exception) {
+            if (!end_fail_soft) {
+                throw;
+            }
+            static u32 dropped{};
+            LOG_ERROR(Render_Vulkan, "Command buffer could not be ended ({}): its work is dropped, tick {} is signalled empty ({} so far)",
+                      exception.what(), signal_value, ++dropped);
+            static constexpr VkCommandBufferBeginInfo EMPTY_BEGIN{
+                .sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_COMMAND_BUFFER_BEGIN_INFO,
+                .pNext = nullptr,
+                .flags = VK_COMMAND_BUFFER_USAGE_ONE_TIME_SUBMIT_BIT,
+                .pInheritanceInfo = nullptr,
+            };
+            // The pool resets a buffer when it begins again, so the two that failed need nothing.
+            upload_cmdbuf = vk::CommandBuffer(command_pool->Commit(), device.GetDispatchLoader());
+            upload_cmdbuf.Begin(EMPTY_BEGIN);
+            upload_cmdbuf.End();
+            cmdbuf = vk::CommandBuffer(command_pool->Commit(), device.GetDispatchLoader());
+            cmdbuf.Begin(EMPTY_BEGIN);
+            cmdbuf.End();
+        }
 
         if (on_submit) {
             on_submit();
